hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27979","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Abd Allah ibn Umayrah, from Durrah bint Abi Lahab, she said: I was with Aishah, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and said: Bring me ablution water. She said: I and Aishah raced to the jug, and I took it. He performed ablution, and raised his sight to me, or his glance to me, and said: You are from me and I am from you. She said: A man was brought, and he said: I did not do it; it was only said to me. She said: And he had asked him upon the pulpit: Who are the best of people. He said: The most versed of them in the religion of Allah, and the most joining of them to kinship. Sharik mentioned therein two other things I did not memorize."
"27980","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd Allah ibn Umayrah, from the husband of Durrah bint Abi Lahab, from Durrah bint Abi Lahab, she said: A man stood to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was upon the pulpit, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of people are the most reciting, and the most God-fearing, and the most enjoining good, and the most forbidding evil, and the most joining to kinship."
